			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845437">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Hello&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Bye&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My main concern is how you're going to be pulling this off. It seems interesting, but it sounds a little cliché like Ramses pointed out.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>3. Greed (Million dollars on the table. Take it or leave it.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What happens if you take it? There should be some sort of punishment.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>5. Wrath (Worst enemy in life, and/or thing that caused a horrible feeling. Supposed to trigger hate.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Will it attack you, or something else? This idea needs to be fleshed-out further, and like I mentioned, adding some sort of punishment.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>6. Envy (Person with something youve always wanted, they leave it out of their sight, working on something)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What if you take it, or what if you want something else, like a job? What would that look like?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>7. Pride (Theres a 1st, 2nd, and 3rd place stand. Get on one, or help someone else on)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Interesting, but there should be a penalty for this one as well.</p>
<p>Overall, the idea is interesting, but&#8230; it's pretty vague and needs stuff like penalties for falling for the tricks and writing it to be less cliché-y.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

